  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-PMR26-IDN103</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive and better managed social security system for all workers</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">During this biennium, activities will emphasize the need for a more inclusive social protection system that effectively covers diverse groups of workers. In particular, efforts to advance reform of the National Social Security System (SJSN) towards a universal, adequate, and sustainable framework will be strengthened through the expansion of employment-based social security coverage for all workers, without exception, including maritime workers, migrant fishers, and platform workers.

Interventions will also support core reforms, including pension and old-age security (JHT) reform, covering fair retirement ages and benefit levels, as well as a mandatory basic pension for the entire population, and the strengthening of unemployment insurance (JKP) through broader coverage, improved benefit adequacy, equitable and sustainable financing, and more effective training and job placement services. To ensure legal certainty and alignment with international standards, the ILO will further promote the integration of key benefits, such as unemployment protection, maternity and sickness benefits, and long-term care, into legislative reforms, including revisions to the SJSN framework and progress towards the ratification of ILO Convention No. 102.

The primary beneficiaries of the ILO&#x2019;s intervention are the social partners, including workers and employers in formal and informal economies. Key stakeholders include institutions and actors involved in social security.</narrative>
  </description>
